# Format of the machine-wide commit-guard denylist read by tools/check-secrets.sh
# and the global git hooks: ~/.config/commit-guard/denylist (outside every repo,
# mode 600). It holds the sensitive literals that are NOT `.env` values, so the
# .env-derived layer can't see them (third-party names, product/brand names,
# anything confidential-but-not-a-config-value).
#
# One literal per line; `#` comments and blank lines ignored. Matched as whole
# words, case-insensitive and accent-insensitive, so distinctive names are safe
# to list.
#
# Placeholders below are OBVIOUSLY FAKE — never put a real value in THIS file
# (it is committed). Real values go only in ~/.config/commit-guard/denylist.

Acme
ExampleCorp
SomeClientName
